# Authored narrative; citations point to individually appraised publications.
TOPICS=[]
def topic(key,title,description,ids,paragraphs):
 TOPICS.append(dict(key=key,title=title,description=description,ids=ids.split(),paragraphs=[p[0] for p in paragraphs],citations=[p[1].split() for p in paragraphs]))
topic('mental-health-map','IL-6 across mental health: the evidence map','A shared research pathway with diagnosis-specific limits.','25133871 37217205 36893912 26903267 32533781',[
('IL-6 is a credible transdiagnostic research pathway, with repeated group-level associations across depression, psychosis, bipolar disorder, PTSD and substance use disorders. That does not establish IL-6 as the core cause of every mental illness, or as abnormal in every affected person. Anxiety and ADHD findings are less consistent. The most useful question is which phenotype, tissue, time course and signalling process is involved, and whether changing that process improves an outcome that matters to people.','36893912 26903267 32533781'),
('This expansion contains 120 peer-reviewed publications: 117 directly relevant mental-health papers and three contextual substance-exposure papers. These are publications, not 120 independent experiments or 120 randomized trials. Reviews reuse primary studies, some reports share cohorts, and several analyses are secondary outcomes from trials. The original 42-source OXTR register remains alongside this expansion; its source types include material beyond peer-reviewed experiments. The combined chapter has 162 distinct source records.',''),
('The hierarchy begins with direct pathway intervention, followed by randomized interventions that measure IL-6, genetic and longitudinal studies, case-control comparisons, and mechanistic work. A treatment RCT can establish an intervention effect without proving that IL-6 mediated it. A meta-analysis can strengthen evidence for an association while inheriting confounding from the studies it pools. A genetic instrument can help test causality, but is not equivalent to a prescription or a short-term change in blood IL-6.','42160062 29090685 37217205'),
('Childhood IL-6 preceded later depression and psychotic experiences in ALSPAC, but the estimate for diagnosed psychotic disorder was imprecise. Temporal ordering is useful evidence, not a complete causal demonstration. Similar cohort names across papers signal related evidence rather than new independent populations. No individual diagnostic threshold or reliable suicide-risk classifier is established by this evidence map.','25133871 37779624 33740587')])
topic('depression','Depression: association is stronger than treatment proof','Direct IL-6 receptor trials, adjunctive RCTs, symptoms and genetic evidence.','depression',[
('The most direct test in this set is the 2026 double-blind tocilizumab trial in difficult-to-treat depression with repeatedly elevated CRP. Thirty people were randomized and 29 received an infusion. The primary day-14 somatic outcome was null: adjusted difference −0.12, 95% CI −2.51 to 2.28. Later patterns favouring treatment justify further investigation, but do not establish efficacy. Small descriptive response and remission differences are especially unstable. Baseline CRP, not IL-6, tracked improvement.','42160062'),
('Indirect intervention trials are mixed. A small celecoxib trial improved symptoms and lowered IL-6, while a pentoxifylline study reported changes in several cytokines, including lower IL-10. Conversely, zinc and probiotic studies reported selected clinical or cognitive benefits without IL-6 reductions. A larger ketamine biomarker analysis found no consistent relationship between inflammatory trajectories and improvement. These results separate treatment benefit from a claim that IL-6 suppression is its necessary mechanism.','22516310 30205379 23602205 30388595 40188855'),
('Minocycline illustrates the uncertainty around inflammatory selection. The small CRP-enriched trial was negative overall, with exploratory signals in a higher-CRP subgroup; a separate 71-person trial analysis found no overall IL-6 change. The EPA dose-finding study also missed its prespecified IL-6 target and its clinical response comparisons were nonsignificant. These are research leads, not established biomarker-guided treatment rules.','33504955 34937590 36005883'),
('Observational syntheses repeatedly associate depression with higher IL-6. Longitudinal studies suggest small relationships in both directions: inflammation can precede symptoms, and symptoms can precede inflammation. Fatigue, sleep, appetite and anhedonia do not all share identical associations. Genetic analyses support some IL-6-pathway hypotheses, while HUNT provides imprecise or discordant estimates. Metabolic, behavioural and immune mechanisms may overlap without being interchangeable.','20015486 26065825 32807846 34135474 34505025 37217205'),
('A secondary hyperthermia analysis is a useful biological counterexample: a brief increase in the IL-6-to-soluble-receptor ratio related to later improvement. The authors interpret this as compatible with classical signalling, but the ratio is an indirect measure and the sample is small. This supports testing the timing and type of signalling rather than assuming that every IL-6 increase is harmful. A linked correction notice is retained in the source record.','38677624 33631287')])
topic('psychosis','Schizophrenia and psychosis','Peripheral and central associations; direct blockade remains unproven.','psychosis',[
('The double-blind schizophrenia tocilizumab trial randomized 36 adults and found no benefit on symptoms or cognition. CRP decreased while measured IL-6 increased. This is direct evidence that peripheral target engagement can occur without clinical improvement, and that receptor blockade is not the same as reducing the measured ligand concentration. The result does not settle every early-illness or inflammation-selected population, but it is central counterevidence.','29090685'),
('The 207-person BeneMin trial also found no benefit of minocycline on negative symptoms or plasma IL-6 over 12 months, constraining smaller positive trials. Berberine produced positive findings in an open-label study with substantial attrition and per-protocol analysis. The small inflammation-enriched canakinumab trial targeted IL-1β, with strong CRP changes but limited clinical evidence. None establishes an OXTR-to-IL-6-to-recovery pathway.','30322824 29678772 37069570 37848096'),
('Associations are more consistent than therapeutic results. Medication-naive first-episode studies show IL-6 elevations, reducing the likelihood that antipsychotics explain the entire association. Larger syntheses report elevations in both acute and chronic illness, while earlier reviews found greater state dependence. A CSF meta-analysis also found elevated IL-6, but blood and CSF evidence remain separate and neither measures all brain-cell signalling.','24704219 21641581 36863384 38364730'),
('Clinical-risk groups show a small pooled IL-6 elevation, yet IL-6 did not reliably distinguish future converters from non-converters. Nor does distributional evidence consistently identify a discrete inflammatory subgroup. Stratifying a trial by repeated inflammation measurements is a testable research strategy, not an established biological subtype or a diagnostic tool. Genetic receptor associations add a different evidence layer with their own assumptions.','33740587 30407606 29094161')])
topic('bipolar','Bipolar depression and euthymia','Mood states, medication and biomarker change require separate interpretation.','bipolar-rest',[
('Bipolar depression has several randomized biomarker studies, with mixed or negative clinical results. Pentoxifylline reduced inflammatory markers but did not beat placebo overall. Memantine added to valproate changed TNF but not IL-6 or clinical outcomes between groups. NAC-related analyses likewise did not demonstrate an overall IL-6 reduction. A cytokine response is not automatically a mood response.','39128677 24717258 32600481'),
('The adaptive aspirin/minocycline trial reported response-rate and subgroup signals, while mean depression-score change had no significant main drug effect. Interim design and outcome changes, small cells and exploratory interactions limit certainty. In a separate bipolar II trial analysis, both treatment groups improved while quetiapine plus psychotherapy increased IL-6 relative to psychotherapy plus placebo. This directly challenges a simple model of recovery requiring lower IL-6.','29362444 31920220'),
('Meta-analyses differ on whether IL-6 is predominantly a state or trait marker. The 2021 synthesis found elevations in depressed, manic and euthymic groups, whereas earlier work found less consistent depressed-state differences and no single marker that reliably separated phases. Most comparisons remain between people rather than repeated measurements through all states in the same person.','34332041 30113291 23419545'),
('Euthymia is not absence of all biological change, yet peripheral and central findings can disagree. A small CSF study found lower IL-6 despite higher IL-1β, while another euthymic study found no difference in soluble IL-6 receptor. Receptor concentration, CSF cytokines and blood cytokines are distinct measurements. Medication, adiposity, sleep and recent episode history remain important covariates.','21138659 32871531')])
topic('mania','Mania: state-sensitive and heterogeneous','Positive findings coexist with smaller opposite-direction studies.','19251324 17845274 25451609',[
('Some phase-comparison studies show elevated IL-6 during mania, with less consistent differences during remission. A longitudinal rapid-cycling study found higher IL-6 and IL-18 in manic/hypomanic states than depressed or euthymic states after adjustment. Repeated within-person sampling is particularly useful for testing whether inflammation tracks an episode.','19251324 25451609'),
('An earlier small unmedicated study reported a contrasting manic pattern with lower IL-6 relative to depression. Sample size, episode definition, medication exposure, sleep loss, agitation, smoking and metabolic health can change the observed pattern. The evidence supports heterogeneity rather than an invariant mania marker.','17845274 34332041'),
('A decisive next step is to distinguish onset, peak illness, treatment and recovery within the same participants, with prespecified clinical and immune endpoints. Existing associations do not establish selective IL-6 blockade as a treatment for mania, nor demonstrate that an OXTR-based intervention prevents or resolves manic episodes.','25451609 39128677')])
topic('hypomania','Hypomania: a specific evidence gap','Do not substitute bipolar depression or pooled mania findings for hypomania.','27476619',[
('The clearest dedicated longitudinal lead links higher childhood IL-6 with hypomanic features at age 22 in ALSPAC. The adjusted top-versus-bottom-third odds ratio was 1.77, with a 95% confidence interval of 1.10–2.85. The association persisted after adjustment for depression at 18, but the outcome was a self-report hypomania checklist rather than confirmed bipolar disorder.','27476619'),
('The rapid-cycling study pooled mania and hypomania. It therefore cannot establish a separate hypomania effect size. Bipolar II depression trials study a depressive episode, not the efficacy of IL-6 modulation during hypomania. These distinctions remain visible even when they leave a smaller evidence base.','25451609 24717258'),
('No convincing hypomania-specific IL-6 intervention result was identified in this targeted set. A useful hypothesis is that a subset of episode transitions involves immune change, but prospective replication, precise episode ascertainment and attention to sleep and medication are needed before any clinical inference.','27476619 25451609')])
topic('anxiety','Anxiety disorders: GAD, panic and social anxiety','Diagnosis-specific positive and null findings.','anxiety',[
('Anxiety is not one inflammatory phenotype. In a large NESDA analysis, current anxiety disorders did not show an overall adjusted IL-6 association; social phobia sometimes showed lower values. Panic-disorder meta-analyses report higher IL-6 but with considerable heterogeneity. A broad anxiety-related meta-analysis found that PTSD largely drove the pooled inflammatory result.','23612048 34908836 30199144'),
('The GAD psychotherapy RCT is especially instructive: symptoms improved, but the inflammatory profile did not improve as predicted, and IL-6 increased in the acceptance-based arm. An uncontrolled SSRI cohort showed falling IL-6 and anxiety, but lacks the randomized comparator needed to isolate a medication effect. These designs answer different questions.','38725444 31163212'),
('A social-anxiety study found altered kynurenine metabolism and lower IL-10, without differences in basal or stimulated pro-inflammatory cytokines. Regulatory and metabolic pathways may matter even when IL-6 is not elevated. There is no validated general anxiety IL-6 threshold or established anxiety treatment based on selective IL-6 suppression in this set.','34758380 29241050')])
topic('ptsd','PTSD and trauma','Trauma exposure, disorder, stress reactivity and recovery are distinct.','ptsd',[
('Across meta-analyses, PTSD is associated with higher peripheral IL-6 on average. Effect sizes vary considerably. Whether controls have also experienced trauma matters: some subgroup analyses weaken or remove the difference, while other syntheses retain it. Depression comorbidity, medication, sex, assay and sampling time also affect estimates. Trauma exposure alone is not a PTSD diagnosis.','26544749 32158005 35477973 41115574'),
('Small double-blind cervical vagus-stimulation experiments blocked IL-6 responses to traumatic scripts; a related 20-person pilot also reported symptom improvement. The acute study included only ten people with PTSD, and related reports belong to one research programme rather than multiple independent replications. These device results do not demonstrate oxytocin or OXTR mediation and cannot be transferred directly to music, social interaction or another intervention.','34589887 34778863'),
('Pooled veteran mindfulness trials found no treatment-group difference in IL-6 change, despite clinical improvement. Small stress-challenge cohorts report potential predictive value for IL-6 and IL-10, but samples are too small to establish clinical selection rules. Resting concentration, stress reactivity and recovery kinetics remain different candidate endpoints.','36938380 33988765 36351891 36732491'),
('Trauma-related distress can interact with sleep, metabolic health and behaviour over years. In the Nurses’ Health study analysis, IL-6 associations were clearer cross-sectionally, while the longitudinal signal centred on CRP. The separate DOCK2 chapter remains an exploratory epigenetic research strand; DOCK2, DOC2 and CK2 are different entities, and none establishes the proposed OXTR–IL-6 mechanism in PTSD.','36115323')])
topic('suicidality','Suicidal ideation and behaviour','Association does not establish individual prediction or prevention.','suicidality',[
('Suicidal ideation, attempts and death by suicide are distinct outcomes. Meta-analyses often find higher IL-6 against healthy controls, with smaller or absent differences against psychiatric controls. The 2025 depression-specific synthesis found no significant IL-6 difference between depressed people with and without suicidal behaviour, with extreme heterogeneity. This prevents treating a general depression association as suicide-specific biology.','37356288 41272690 25541493'),
('In veterans, IL-6 tracked ideation severity but did not predict whether ideation was present. NESDA findings differed between ideation alone and attempt history. In psychosis, IL-2 and IL-10 carried the principal longitudinal associations rather than IL-6. Several case-control studies also found null or confounder-sensitive IL-6 results.','37779624 35202735 38549611 33388702 30844329'),
('Specimen and timing can reverse interpretation. One synthesis reported serum/CSF elevations but lower plasma IL-6, with a numerical inconsistency in its abstract that is flagged in the register. Recent injury, infection, acute stress, toxic exposure and postmortem processes can influence cytokines around an attempt or death. Such measurements are not automatically premorbid risk markers.','34280025 25541493 34730074'),
('Genetic evidence linking IL-6 signalling to a suicidality symptom is a mechanistic lead, not proof that IL-6 blockade prevents suicide. No clinical suicide-prediction test or prevention claim is made here. Future intervention research needs direct clinical outcomes and appropriate clinical oversight rather than substituting a blood-marker change for reduced risk.','33079133 37356288')])
topic('adhd','ADHD: a mixed and developing literature','Paediatric findings, adult null results and intervention limits.','adhd',[
('ADHD is a neurodevelopmental condition. Its IL-6 literature is smaller and less consistent than the depression or psychosis literature. A 2021 synthesis found no significant IL-6 difference; a 2022 synthesis found an elevation that lost significance when individual studies were removed. A 2026 network meta-analysis highlighted elevated IL-6 for autism, while ADHD findings centred on other markers. Autism results are not ADHD results.','34413283 35660454 42287409'),
('The randomized evidence also conflicts. An older omega-3 trial reported reduced IL-6 and improved parent ratings. Vitamin D did not reduce IL-6 relative to placebo. In a probiotic pilot, IL-6 decreased in both arms, so that change was not specific to the probiotic. None establishes IL-6 as a routine ADHD treatment target or demonstrates an OXTR mechanism.','24568073 36052304 32256407'),
('Some child and adolescent case-control studies show higher IL-6, sometimes without a relationship to symptom severity. An unmedicated adult study found no case-control IL-6 difference. Small samples, age, asthma, obesity, sleep, medication and comorbid behavioural conditions may contribute to disagreement. Cytokine findings from childhood cannot automatically be generalized to adults.','33936305 30430896 37511467 28262601 34371132'),
('Prospective pregnancy and childhood-sleep studies offer developmental hypotheses. The maternal study used a multi-cytokine composite, so its effect cannot be attributed solely to IL-6. ALSPAC reported statistical mediation between early sleep problems and probable ADHD, but observational mediation is not a causal experiment. A prevention or treatment claim remains premature.','32707260 36597271 20534153 35197458')])
topic('alcohol','Alcohol use disorder','Exposure, withdrawal and recovery produce different immune patterns.','40305022 35754106 40630018 35995431 15282117 31736187 31541874 37484196',[
('The 102-person, double-masked ibudilast trial found no benefit on heavy drinking and no peripheral inflammatory-marker effect. Its earlier two-week biomarker trial produced selected, often nominal signals; those findings did not establish a specific IL-6 mechanism and did not replicate as overall efficacy in the larger trial. Exenatide also failed to change inflammatory biomarkers in a post hoc AUD trial analysis.','40305022 35754106 40630018'),
('The alcohol-specific meta-analysis found moderately higher IL-6, while thirteen other cytokines were not significantly different. A study excluding liver disease also reported elevated IL-6, showing that liver pathology is not the only possible explanation. Nonetheless, active drinking, withdrawal duration, nutrition, infection, smoking, adiposity and liver health all need attention in an individual study.','35995431 15282117'),
('Lower is not always better: blunted IL-6 stress responses predicted more subsequent drinking in one alcohol-dependent cohort. Cue experiments in binge drinkers linked greater IL-6 reactivity to craving and later consumption, but did not test a treatment for diagnosed AUD. In a CBM trial, IL-6 was below assay detection and was unavailable for analysis; that is an assay limit, not proof of zero inflammation.','31736187 37484196 31541874'),
('The systems-biology hypothesis therefore concerns dysregulated timing and coordination, not a single universally high cytokine. Clinical recovery, sustained drinking outcomes and functioning remain primary questions. An OXTR-based intervention can be investigated as a separate hypothesis, with no current evidence that its IL-6 effect treats AUD.','40305022 31736187')])
topic('opioids','Opioid use disorder','Treatment cohorts and small intervention studies.','33719920 25988317 25716777 31513981 30071446 25660662 36181736',[
('Memantine and dextromethorphan adjunct trials during methadone treatment reported selected treatment and immune findings, mainly involving TNF or regulatory markers. They did not establish a selective IL-6 mechanism. A very small sham-controlled tDCS study improved impulsivity but did not significantly reduce IL-6. A double-blind label is recorded separately from confirmation of random allocation.','25988317 25716777 33719920'),
('Prospective cohorts associate higher IL-6 with poorer methadone-treatment outcomes and poorer memory or executive performance. Continued opioid exposure can also drive inflammatory change, creating reverse causation. Attrition was substantial in some studies, and related regional cohorts may overlap. These findings support investigation, not a validated relapse predictor.','31513981 30071446 36181736'),
('Methadone-dose correlations do not establish that methadone causes inflammation: dose reflects clinical need and prior exposure. Infection, injection-related injury, pain, smoking, other substances and social conditions may confound comparisons. Effective addiction treatment and an experimental cytokine hypothesis are separate clinical questions.','25660662 31513981')])
topic('stimulants','Stimulant use disorders: cocaine and methamphetamine','Inflammatory signals are neither uniform nor synonymous with relapse reduction.','34331010 31812878 34432333 31749792 39504756 37424424',[
('An exploratory CBD analysis in cocaine use disorder reported lower IL-6, but a biomarker result alone does not demonstrate abstinence or relapse prevention. A small ibudilast methamphetamine challenge study attenuated selected inflammatory measures; its positive treatment findings did not establish suppression of the later IL-6 response.','34331010 31812878'),
('Methamphetamine case-control findings conflict: one study found higher IL-6 and associations with depressive symptoms, while another found no IL-6 difference despite oxidative and blood-cell abnormalities. Cocaine withdrawal studies also distinguish stimulated immune-cell secretion from resting blood concentrations. Substances, withdrawal stage and laboratory methods all matter.','34432333 37424424 31749792'),
('A randomized contingency-management study provides another counterexample: the group with the largest cocaine-use reduction showed increased IL-6 and decreased IL-10. Immune recovery can involve changed responsiveness rather than monotonic cytokine suppression. This makes functional outcomes and repeated measures more informative than a single desired biomarker direction.','39504756')])
topic('cannabis-nicotine','Cannabis and nicotine: contextual evidence and gaps','Exposure studies are not trials of diagnosed use disorders.','32554630 25274579',[
('The two contextual papers retained here concern cannabis exposure in people with and without HIV, and cigarette smoking in older adults. Neither establishes IL-6 as a causal pathway in cannabis-use disorder or nicotine dependence. These papers are excluded from the 117 directly relevant mental-health count. The third contextual paper is the binge-drinking cue experiment.','32554630 25274579 37484196'),
('The cannabis study’s main associations involved other inflammatory markers and composites, not a demonstrated IL-6 treatment effect. HIV and compartment-specific biology limit transfer to other populations. It provides no basis for claiming cannabis treats inflammation-related mental illness.','32554630'),
('Smoking was associated with a mixed immune profile, including higher CRP and lower soluble IL-6 receptor. Tobacco exposure is therefore an important confounder in psychiatric cytokine studies. Nicotine, combustion products, smoking behaviour and dependence are distinct exposures; this targeted review leaves disorder-specific intervention gaps explicit.','25274579')])
topic('systems-hypothesis','From OXTR to mental-health outcomes: a testable hypothesis','Separate each link in the proposed causal chain.','',[
('A plausible systems model connects a defined intervention to OXTR-related signalling, immune regulation, neural or behavioural change, and meaningful clinical outcomes. The existing cell and animal OXTR literature supports selected links. The mental-health literature supports IL-6 associations and some pathway hypotheses. Combining those literatures creates a research hypothesis; it does not complete the causal chain in humans.','18940936 28049625 18593851 42160062 29090685'),
('IL-6 can signal through membrane-bound IL-6 receptor and gp130, or through soluble-receptor complexes acting on gp130-expressing cells. Soluble gp130 provides important regulation of trans-signalling. Receptor blockade, lower ligand concentration, altered receptor shedding and altered cell responsiveness are different perturbations. Human IL-6 administration can also raise IL-10 and IL-1RA, demonstrating that pro-inflammatory and regulatory responses are linked.','11121117 12857678 38677624 29090685'),
('For Universal Mind, a defensible question is whether a precisely defined intervention changes repeated IL-6-related measures and clinical outcomes, and whether OXTR-related biology contributes. Use a suitable comparator, prespecified outcomes, realistic masking, repeated baseline samples and a prespecified analysis of inflammation-related variation. Measure clinical benefit separately from biomarkers; a mediation analysis needs appropriate timing and assumptions and remains weaker than direct pathway perturbation.','42160062 30322824 40305022'),
('A practical exploratory panel can include IL-6, hs-CRP, TNF, IL-1β, IL-10 and IL-1RA, with sIL-6R and soluble gp130 when the signalling question justifies them. Record detection limits, specimen type, collection time, recent infection, BMI, smoking, sleep, medication and substance exposure. IL-10 is regulatory, CRP is an acute-phase marker, and neither has a universally desirable direction. Lower IL6 RNA, lower circulating protein and lower pathway activity are not interchangeable endpoints.','31541874 25451609 25274579 38725444 12857678'),
('Measure OXTR-related endpoints with cell-type and assay specificity. Plasma oxytocin, OXTR methylation and receptor expression do not prove receptor activation in the brain. No included paper validates the combined Universal Mind intervention–OXTR–IL-6–mental-health-benefit chain. The opportunity is a focused, transparent human research programme; any claim of global novelty needs a separate, protocol-specific search.','23899661 37360277 41239825 42160062')])
topic('mental-health-method','Review method, quality and remaining gaps','Transparent source counts, access depth and limits.','',[
('Searches and identifier checks were conducted on 28 November 2026 using public PubMed/Europe PMC records, publisher pages and accessible full text, with trial-first, diagnosis-specific and contradictory-result searches. The register contains 120 unique peer-reviewed publications, including 117 directly relevant mental-health papers and three contextual exposure papers. Protocols, registry entries, preprints and correction notices are not counted as new publications in this expansion.',''),
('This is a structured narrative evidence map, not a registered systematic review, an exhaustive database search, an individual-participant meta-analysis or a formal GRADE assessment. Searches were bounded and selection was purposive. All included abstracts were appraised; selected available full-text methods and results were checked for pivotal trials. Each record states access depth. Linked correction notices remain attached, with unresolved correction content explicitly flagged.',''),
('Nature-family, Frontiers and other specialist journals are represented, together with veteran and Navy-associated research. PubMed/NIH indexing and a government domain aid traceability; they do not guarantee low bias. Sample size, randomization, masking, outcome prespecification, attrition, comparator, confounding, multiplicity and replication carry more weight than a publisher or domain name. Publication Trust Factor is study-design shorthand, not a clinical-efficacy or certainty grade.','34589887 37779624 36938380'),
('The companion register retains original identifiers, individual findings, limitations, trial/cohort-family links and bibliographic provenance. Reviews overlap primary studies. Where cohort independence, masking or a correction cannot be resolved, uncertainty remains visible. The website-wide JSON/CSV snapshots and Universal One use the same appraised records. Updating Universal One means versioned retrieval knowledge; it does not mean that model weights were fine-tuned.','')])
